From 0e4576e0b6e6772804ee5dbc417aea98f34fc851 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GPU3D: the JIT's STMs into the GX FIFO in one call, with
 0060's loop

render.gx_batch (MELONDS_GXBATCH=0 turns it off; default on). Session 2's patch 0021 (memio), ported onto 0060-0071
(renumbered 0063). Games send display lists to the GX FIFO (0x04000400-0x0400043F) with STMs (NitroSDK's
GX_SendFifo*, MI_CpuSend32); each went through SlowBlockTransfer9's general checks, then GPU3D::WriteToGXFIFO ->
WriteToGXFIFOBody per word: a call and a 4-register-pair frame per word, the packed command's state loaded and
stored per word, and CmdFIFOWriteFast's FIFO count, write position and GXSTAT per entry.
- SlowBlockTransfer9 checks for an STM into the GX FIFO first, with the same conditions as its block path (the GX
  route and memfast IO on, clear of the TCMs, all words in 0x04000400-0x0400043F; not with MELONDS_IOSTATS), and
  hands the words to GPU3D::WriteGXFIFOWords; everything else goes on to the unchanged body (a tail call).
- WriteGXFIFOWords runs patch 0060's block loop (now WriteGXFIFOWordsFast, shared with WriteGXFIFOBlock, the GX
  FIFO DMA's path) over the STM's words: the command state and the FIFO's level and write position in registers,
  GXSTAT's bits and the push/pop and test counts set at the end; an entry into an empty or full FIFO takes
  CmdFIFOWriteFast. Unlike the DMA's block, the words go on after one that stalls the system (as word by word: a
  full FIFO puts each in the stall queue). Without GeomFast, WriteToGXFIFOBody<false> per word, as before.
Session 2's version had a loop of its own and also hooked the DMA's block path; 0060 already does that, so this
reuses 0060's loop instead (FIFO.h's extra accessors are not needed).

Exact: the JIT charges an STM's cycles in its code, and the words reach the FIFO, the pipe and the stall queue in
the same order with the same GXSTAT.
